<report>
<line><title>Indirectly Standardized Rates and SMR</title></line>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><th>Reference rate</th><th>Observed person-time</th><th>Expected deaths</th><th></th></tr>
<tr><td><block name="groups"><in>group</in></td><td><in>observed</in></td><td><in>expected</in></td><td><in>lb</in></td></tr>
<tr><td></block></td><td></td><td>Total = <in>total</in></td><td></td></tr>
</table>
<line></line>
<line>Standardized Mortality Ratio (SMR) = <in>ratio</in></line>
<line><b>SMR (*100 as integer) = <in>smr</in></b></line>
<line><ci>Exact <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>from</in> to <in>to</in> (<in>from100</in> to <in>to100</in>)</ci></line>
<line></line>
<line><pval>Probability of observing <in>qty</in> or more deaths by chance <in>p_hi</in></pval></line>
<line><pval>Probability of observing <in>qty</in> or fewer deaths by chance <in>p_lo</in></pval></line>
</report>
